{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → acc 0.485, F1 0.464), the evidence is extremely sparse and the performance is near chance. The most critical uncertainty is whether the low performance is specific to the RNA modality/encoding or reflects a broader task difficulty. config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) tests the simplest image-only configuration with a well-established pretrained encoder, providing a clean baseline for the image modality. This is the most informative next step because: (1) it isolates the effect of modality (image vs RNA) while keeping the profile setting (singleprofile) and complexity (no aggregation/fusion) minimal, (2) it establishes whether image features carry useful signal for this classification task, which directly informs whether any multimodal configuration is worth pursuing, and (3) it broadens our understanding of the design space before committing to deeper exploration within one modality. If image performs substantially better, the bottleneck is RNA encoding; if it also performs poorly, the task or data may be the limiting factor. Either outcome sharply reduces uncertainty for all subsequent decisions."
}

